gadget: remove CDC ACM from the composite (UVC only)

Opening the ACM tty from the host was reproducibly observed to transition the
shared BCM2835 DWC2 gadget into a persistent bad UVC isochronous state (choppy
video / -ENODATA), on both the baseline and later builds. Remove the ACM
function/endpoints entirely so the host cannot enumerate/open it.

Signed-off-by: webcampi <webcampi@localhost>

--- a/scripts/uvc-gadget.sh
+++ b/scripts/uvc-gadget.sh
@@ -174,10 +174,9 @@
 	mkdir configs/c.1
 	mkdir configs/c.1/strings/0x409
 
-        echo "Creating serial console..."
-        mkdir functions/acm.usb0
-        ln -s functions/acm.usb0 configs/c.1/
-        echo "OK"
+	# No CDC ACM serial console: opening the ACM tty from the host was shown to
+	# persistently degrade UVC isochronous streaming on the shared DWC2 gadget.
+	# Composite is UVC only for this step.
 
 	echo "Creating functions..."
 	create_uvc configs/c.1 uvc.0
